{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>These are the heads of their fathers' houses</b> — Scripture did not wish to begin 'these are the names of the sons of Levi according to their generations' (לתלדותם), lest it appear that Levi is the firstborn of the genealogy from here onward, for the honor of Moses. Rather, it mentioned his brothers who were older than him, and he is counted third. And in the sons of Levi it mentioned 'their generations' (לתולדותם), because for Reuben and Simeon it mentioned only those who went down to Egypt with them, whereas for Levi it mentions his generations and his years and the generations of the fathers of the prophets and their years, in their honor. And furthermore, because they themselves were pious men of the Most High, worthy of being recounted through, like the fathers of the world."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:42.813957720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}